{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AgDAYTNy2dXbrR4VX5RbGP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# docs/stack.ini — the kit meta-repo's own product toolchain, declared once.\n2\t#\n3\t# The \"product\" this repo builds is the kit under project-trajectory/; its tests\n4\t# live in tests/ (they bootstrap a real scaffold and exercise every script). This\n5\t# is the meta-repo's SELF-adoption of the process it ships — IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md\n6\t# Thread 47. scripts under project-trajectory/scripts/check.py read this file.\n7\t\n8\t[paths]\n9\tsrc = project-trajectory/scripts\n10\ttests = tests\n11\t\n12\t[product]\n13\tformat = {py} -m ruff format --check {src} {tests}\n14\tlint = {py} -m ruff check {src} {tests}\n15\t# `-n auto` runs the suite across all cores via pytest-xdist (WI-075). Every test\n16\t# is isolated in tmp_path and the meta-tree readers are read-only, so the suite is\n17\t# xdist-safe; subprocess coverage (tests/conftest.augment_env) holds per-worker\n18\t# (measured combined total 90.8%, unchanged from serial). Measured 2026-07-22 on\n19\t# a 24-core box: ~250 s parallel for the full 1374-test suite (~200 s for the\n20\t# smoke tier); the coverage step runs several times longer. These are snapshots,\n21\t# not contracts — re-measure locally before budgeting against them (the prior\n22\t# ~65 s figure predated the v4 dispatch/integrate suite growth and misled\n23\t# session budgeting for weeks; repo-review 2026-07-21 M-24).\n24\t# The `smoke` tier stays as declared; the coverage args below still apply.\n25\ttest = {py} -m pytest -q -n auto\n26\t\n27\t[tiers]\n28\tsmoke = -m smoke\n29\tfull = -m \"not release\"\n30\trelease =\n31\tall =\n32\t\n33\t[coverage]\n34\t# Subprocess coverage IS wired (Thread 47 Phase 6). This suite exercises the kit\n35\t# scripts as SUBPROCESSES (bootstrap a temp scaffold, run the real command), which\n36\t# `--cov` would otherwise miss, so tests/conftest.run_py starts coverage in each\n37\t#